Subject: [PATCH] docs(r48b): phase 2 gate + routing verified, correctness
 receipts, report section 11

Reviewed the phase-2 draft (WIP dccbe3383) against the mandate's rules A and B and
measured it. The draft needed no correction: the per-(type, NUM_COLS) hoist gate and
the MMVQ routing already match the mandate, so this commit adds no code change and
carries the verification, the receipts and report section 11.

Verified:
- Rule A. mmvq_a_hoist_legacy(i) = (i+1 >= 6) ? 0 : mmvq_a_hoist gates the legacy-block
  family (Q4_0/Q4_1/Q5_0/Q5_1/Q8_0/MXFP4) OFF at NUM_COLS >= 6; Q4_K/Q5_K/SX8 stay ON at
  every width; every other type keeps its current setting. GGML_ARIFI_MMVQ_A_HOIST=0
  still forces all OFF, confirmed by the device stderr receipt, not by reading.
- Rule B. S-X8 -> MMVQ at every n by default (GGML_ARIFI_SX8_MMVQ=0 hands it back);
  Q4_K n>=5 -> MMVQ when k <= 8192; Q5_K and Q8_0/legacy unchanged;
  GGML_ARIFI_MMVQ_ROUTE=legacy restores the pre-R48b rules while KEEPING the hoisted nest.

HQ's 14:30 "crash" explained and refuted. Both offered hypotheses are wrong: the gate is
correctly NOT applied to q2_0_g128 (line 7207 passes the bare constant, that type is not in
the legacy family), and the new routing sends nothing to MMVQ without a pipeline (q2_0_g128
at n>1 takes the pre-existing batch return and its q8_1 pipeline exists at every width).
The same row passed in the completed phase-1 sweep and does not reproduce now (62-*, rc=0).
Root cause was parent-process teardown taking the child with it - the rc of 127 beside 89 KB
of passing output is incoherent as a test result. The same mechanism reproduced twice more
in this session at the 10-minute tool cap, kept as 63-mulmat-default-KILLED-BY-WRAPPER-CAP.txt.

Correctness, all synchronous, 0 FAIL on every arm:
- full -o MUL_MAT -b Vulkan0 at defaults, taken as regex-partitioned chunks and then proved
  equal to the phase-1 sweep by set difference: 2879 unique rows, 0 missing (63a-63o, 64)
- sx8 and q4_K each at defaults, GGML_ARIFI_MMVQ_ROUTE=legacy and GGML_ARIFI_MMVQ_A_HOIST=0
  (64-68)
- S-X8 independent-reference slice, a separate mode the MUL_MAT sweep never enters: the
  widened n=4..8 cases are present and on the MMVQ route, 64 cases 0 failed 0 route mismatch.
  Taken on three arms so both routes are scored with the witness live, since on the default
  arm every q8_1 case is route-INFERRED and the mismatch check is inert there (69a-69c).

Origin: fork-authored (ArifiLabs lane-235 R48b phase 2, Opus 5 MEDIUM kernel-maker)
Measured-effect: UNMEASURED at default routing - forced-route pairing: S-X8 flat at the bus n=1..8 (+40..+110% at n>=4 on 248320x5120), q4_K n=6/7 tail cliff removed (5->52 GB/s), q4_K k=5120 n>=5 +21..+57%; default-route re-pair owed to HQ
Lane: lane-235
