+## 11. Phase 2 - gate and routing
+
+Phase 2 adds the per-(type, NUM_COLS) hoist gate and the routing that depends on it, on top of the
+phase-1 hoist (`19da7c2f9`). Files: `ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/ggml-vulkan.cpp`,
+`tests/test-backend-ops.cpp`, `docs/OPTIONS-REGISTRY.md`. The shader is UNCHANGED in phase 2.
+
+### 11.1 The 14:30 "crash" was parent teardown, not a device fault
+
+HQ recorded `r48b-evidence/61-mulmat-default.txt` ending mid-row at
+`MUL_MAT(type_a=q2_0_g128,type_b=f32,m=5120,n=8,k=17408,...): ` with no verdict and the process
+gone, and asked whether the gate or the new routing had sent that type somewhere it had no pipeline.
+Both hypotheses are REFUTED, and the row does not reproduce:
+
+| Question | Finding | Evidence |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| Is the `NUM_COLS >= 6` gate applied to the pipeline the selector picks for `q2_0_g128`? | NO, and correctly so. Line 7207 passes the bare `mmvq_a_hoist`, not `mmvq_a_hoist_legacy(i)`. `Q2_0_G128` is not in the legacy-block family; mandate rule A leaves it on the device-level gate. Phase 2 changes NOTHING for this type's pipelines. | `ggml-vulkan.cpp:7207` vs `7208-7214` |
+| Does the new routing send a type to MMVQ with no `q8_1` pipeline at that width? | NO. `q2_0_g128` at `n > 1` on AMD falls through to the pre-existing "MMVQ is generally good for batches" return, untouched by phase 2, and its `q8_1` pipeline is registered for every `i` in the same loop. | `ggml-vulkan.cpp:7207`, `should_use_mmvq` `n > 1` return |
+| Did the same row pass before? | YES, in the completed phase-1 sweep. | `10-mulmat-hoist-on.txt:922`, 2935 rows, 0 FAIL |
+| Was the binary stale? | NO. `test-backend-ops.exe` is 14:26:52, both edited sources are 14:21:58 / 14:23:44 - run 61 DID exercise phase-2 code. A rebuild confirms "ninja: no work to do". | `60-build.txt` rc=0 |
+| Does it reproduce? | NO. `-p "type_a=q2_0_g128,type_b=f32,m=5120,n=8"` is OK, rc=0. | `62-repro-g128-n8.txt` |
+
+**Root cause: the sweep's parent process was killed at 14:30 and took the child with it** - the same
+session exit that left the maker's report and commit unwritten (the WIP commit is 14:31:33). The
+`.rc` of `127` is incoherent as a test result beside 89 KB of passing output and no FAIL, and fits a
+wrapper writing an rc for a child it had already lost. This mechanism reproduced **twice more in
+this session**: a full unchunked sweep and two later chunks were killed at exactly the 10-minute
+tool cap with identical mid-row truncation and no verdict (`exit 143`). Kept as
+`63-mulmat-default-KILLED-BY-WRAPPER-CAP.txt` - a receipt of the mechanism, not of a defect. No
+device loss, no driver message, nothing to fix in the kernel.
+
+### 11.2 The gate (rule A) - verified as drafted
+
+`mmvq_a_hoist_legacy(i) = (i + 1 >= 6) ? 0 : mmvq_a_hoist`, applied at pipeline creation. With
+`i` in `[0, 7]` and `NUM_COLS == i + 1`, that is OFF at NUM_COLS 6, 7, 8 and unchanged below.
+
+| Family | Types | Hoist constant | Rule A |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| Measured WINNERS | `Q4_K`, `Q5_K`, `SX8` | `mmvq_a_hoist` (every NUM_COLS) | ON everywhere - as mandated |
+| Legacy-block | `Q4_0`, `Q4_1`, `Q5_0`, `Q5_1`, `Q8_0`, `MXFP4` | `mmvq_a_hoist_legacy(i)` | OFF at NUM_COLS >= 6 - as mandated |
+| Everything else | `Q2_0`, `Q2_0_G128`, `Q2_K`, `Q3_K`, `Q6_K`, `ROCMFP4_FAST` | `mmvq_a_hoist` | current setting kept - as mandated |
+| IQ1 | `IQ1_S`, `IQ1_M` | `mmvq_a_hoist_iq1` | phase-1 behaviour, OFF by default |
+
+`GGML_ARIFI_MMVQ_A_HOIST=0` still forces ALL of it off: `mmvq_a_hoist` is 0, so
+`mmvq_a_hoist_legacy()` returns 0 on both arms of its ternary and the IQ1 variable is clamped to 0.
+CHECKED on the device, not read: `66-sx8-hoist-off.txt` prints
+`mmvq A-side hoist: OFF (GGML_ARIFI_MMVQ_A_HOIST) (iq1: OFF) (route: r48b)`.
+
+The gate is measured on `Q8_0` ONLY (`-25 / -17 / -24%` at n=6/7/8 on 4096x14336) and widened to the
+five types that share its register footprint and row count. That widening is stated, not hidden: it
+is a footprint argument from report section 3, not five more measurements.
+
+One structural change carried from the draft and kept: the hoist state is probed ONCE in
+`ggml_vk_get_device()` and stored on the device, not re-derived in `ggml_vk_load_shaders()`. Two
+consumers now need one answer - pipeline creation (entered lazily for a single requested pipeline)
+and `ggml_vk_should_use_mmvq()`. A per-call probe could route a tensor to MMVQ while the pipeline in
+hand was compiled with the inherited nest. That would still be bit-correct, so **no correctness test
+could ever catch it** - which is precisely why it is structural rather than defensive.
+
+### 11.3 The routing (rule B) - verified as drafted
+
+| Rule | Default (R48b) | `GGML_ARIFI_MMVQ_ROUTE=legacy` | `GGML_ARIFI_MMVQ_A_HOIST=0` |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| (i) `SX8` | MMVQ at EVERY n; `GGML_ARIFI_SX8_MMVQ=0` hands it back | opt-in, `=1` only | legacy rules (hoist gone too) |
+| (ii) `Q4_K` n>=5 | MMVQ when `k <= 8192`, f32 above | f32 at every n>=5 | f32 at every n>=5 |
+| (iii) `Q5_K` | unchanged (n=1 MMVQ, n>1 f32) | unchanged | unchanged |
+| (iv) `Q8_0` / legacy | unchanged | unchanged | unchanged |
+
+The three switches are NOT the same arm and a pairing log must say which it used:
+`GGML_ARIFI_SX8_MMVQ=0` moves one type, `GGML_ARIFI_MMVQ_ROUTE=legacy` moves the routing while
+KEEPING the hoisted nest, and `GGML_ARIFI_MMVQ_A_HOIST=0` removes the nest and with it the routing.
+All three are CHECKED on the device via the stderr receipt line, not asserted.
+
+**Superseded lane-198 / lane-230 comment lines, and why the data allows it.** The S-X8 opt-in
+paragraph is superseded *by its own closing sentence*: it predicted "a `NUM_COLS == 7` tail defect in
+the mmvq framework rather than a tuning loss" and said a narrowed admit "starts there". R48b found
+exactly that defect - the nest re-ran the whole A-side decode once per column - and the hoist removes
+it. Under forced MMVQ with the hoist ON, S-X8 is flat at the bus at n=1..8 (248320x5120:
+`74.8/75.2/72.1/73.6/74.2/74.7/73.7/72.8` GB/s) against `62/70/33.5/45.5` at n=5..8 with it OFF. The
+n=7 cliff the opt-in was written around no longer exists on this path, so the reason for the opt-in
+is gone. The lane-198 `Q4_K n>=5` exile is superseded CONDITIONALLY only - on the hoist being live
+AND `k <= 8192` - because the win is k-dependent and reverses at k=17408. `k = 8192` is the midpoint
+of the two measured k values and is named an **untested boundary**: nothing was run between 5120 and
+17408. The lane-198 `Q5_K` line is NOT superseded; its only MMVQ width is n=1 and there the hoist is
+a wash, so widening it would be a guess.
+
+### 11.4 Correctness (rule C) - 0 FAIL on every arm
+
+All synchronous, WinLibs mingw64 `bin` first on PATH, AMD Radeon 780M, `test-backend-ops.exe`
+built at 14:26:52 from the sources hashed in section 11.6.
+
+The full `-o MUL_MAT -b Vulkan0` sweep exceeds the 10-minute tool cap, so it was taken as
+**regex-partitioned chunks over `-p "type_a=(...)"`** (the `-p` filter is `std::regex_search` over
+each case's `vars()`). Coverage was then proved equal to the phase-1 sweep by set difference, not
+assumed: **2879 unique rows, `comm -23` against `10-mulmat-hoist-on.txt` = 0 missing.** One row
+(`iq1_m` n=9) was initially missed by a width filter, detected by that diff, and run separately as
+`63o`.
+
+| Arm | Command | Rows | FAIL | Receipt |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
