+### 11.5 The S-X8 independent reference at n=4..8 (rule C, B2 route check)
+
+The reference slice is a SEPARATE mode (`test-backend-ops sx8ref`) that `-o MUL_MAT` never enters,
+so reading the widened case list off the diff would not have been a receipt. It was run.
+
+Phase 2 widens the case list from `{1,2,3,4,8}` to every mat-vec width, because n=5,6,7 were
+previously unreachable on this path and therefore **never checked against an independent reference**.
+Confirmed on the device: **64 cases, 0 declined, 0 failed, 0 route mismatch, 0 nonfinite**, with
+n=4..8 present on the q8_1 route in both the `m1` and `f32-twin` groups.
+
+| Arm | Route split | INFERRED | Witness | FAIL | Receipt |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| defaults | 40 q8_1 / 24 dequant | 40 | disabled (see below) | 0 | `69a-sx8ref-default.txt` |
+| `GGML_VK_FORCE_MMVQ=1` | 40 q8_1 / 24 dequant | 0 | **live** | 0 | `69b-sx8ref-forced-q8_1.txt` |
